DESCRIPTION:The evening checkpoint was delivered. Desktop field\ncore-web-
 vitals on the main section failed and worsened\, and\na deep performance 
 dive was proposed\, not applied. Indexing\nfor one paper page remains 
 blocked by a crawler-side fetch\nfailure rather than request volume\; the 
 remaining indexing\nqueue is effectively exhausted. A discrepancy between 
 two\ndays' top-paper lists was flagged to reconcile before the\nMonday 
 rotation review. No fixes were applied.
DTSTAMP:20261108T172913Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261015T004700
DURATION:PT20M
SUMMARY:Daily chat archives: published to GitHub\; Drive mirror failed\; 
 one day missing
UID:d973e5be-c71a-455e-a127-ca55d8a3c14d@d973.org
DESCRIPTION:The prior day's main chat archive was exported and 
 published\nto its GitHub repo\, and the companion agent's archive 
 run\ncompleted with no activity that day. The Drive mirror failed\nagain 
 because its folder sits on a permanently disabled\naccount\; repointing it
  awaits the user's decision. A gap was\nfound and flagged: one earlier 
 day's main-chat archive is\nmissing entirely and a directed backfill is 
 still owed.
DTSTAMP:20261108T172913Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261015T000000
DURATION:PT30M
SUMMARY:MapleScholar morning investigation: Ads day blocked on session
UID:3245d309-7f8c-436e-9d49-cc2af0c49022@3245.org
DESCRIPTION:The Ads-email sweep completed through the mail connector 
 and\nfound only informational notices\, no campaign action. The\nbrowser 
 session check found every account challenged and none\nlive\, so the in-
 product sweep and the full Ads deep dive were\nblocked and unverified\; 
 prior baselines were carried\, not\npresented as today's data. No changes 
 were made anywhere.\nOwner re-sign-in is the only route forward.
DTSTAMP:20261108T172913Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261015T072500
DURATION:PT30M
SUMMARY:Job search rules overhauled: skill-first three-track method adopted
UID:b71dddad-aadd-457b-bf10-37f4c68e52cd@b71d.org
DESCRIPTION:At the user's direction\, the job search method was 
 rebuilt:\nmatching is now on skills and duties\, not titles or 
 seniority\,\nwith three separate tracks reported separately (contract 
 and\nplatform work\, career roles\, and stable health\, research 
 and\nnonprofit roles)\, a skill-first keyword set\, a per-city\nlocation 
 rule for platform searches\, and a rule that every\napplication is shown 
 in final form and sent only after the\nuser's approval. The daily sweep 
 was rewritten to match.
DTSTAMP:20261108T172913Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261015T075000
DURATION:PT45M
SUMMARY:Job search rerun completed: merged three-track lists delivered
UID:f83f7173-61ef-4b7c-86e3-8f177d8922c6@f83f.org
DESCRIPTION:The existing verified pool was reclassified under the 
 new\nthree-track rules and fresh skill-first platform searches were\nrun\,
  completing the rerun. Track A grew to a dozen verified\ncontract 
 candidates and Track C to over thirty entries\, with\nTrack B remaining 
 the hardest track. The merged lists were\ndelivered to the user. Two roles
  closing the next day were\nflagged as time-sensitive for his decision.
DTSTAMP:20261108T172913Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261015T080000
DURATION:PT20M
SUMMARY:Outside job-search demonstration reviewed
UID:bb61d976-bda8-4830-8777-53bf6e7b8c64@bb61.org
DESCRIPTION:The user shared an outside job-search demonstration 
 document\nfor review. Assessment delivered: its method was 
 disciplined\nbut it was a sample\, not a systematic sweep. It surfaced 
 a\nfew leads the agent's own searches had missed\; those are held\npending
  verification on the employers' own sites before they\nenter the lists. 
 One keyword lesson from it was adopted.
DTSTAMP:20261108T172913Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261015T090000
DURATION:PT30M
SUMMARY:Oct 8 application batch: follow-up drafts delivered\, nothing sent
UID:553bded4-68af-4ab7-acbe-78899a5caa91@553b.org
DESCRIPTION:The seven-day follow-up run for the thirteen October 
 8\napplications prepared thirteen individual follow-up drafts\,\ndelivered
  to the user for approval\; nothing was sent. Employer\nchecks found no 
 replies\, rejections\, or interview invites\nsince the original 
 confirmations. One employer's repeated\nincomplete-application reminders 
 were clarified as relating\nto a separate referral never applied to\, not 
 to the submitted\napplication\; that decision rests with the user.
DTSTAMP:20261108T172913Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261015T090100
DURATION:PT30M
SUMMARY:Proactive deliveries: two corrections\, a security alert\, grant 
 drafts complete
UID:e248b49b-149e-459e-a201-8637eed9ab53@e248.org
DESCRIPTION:Corrections were delivered: two previously flagged items 
 are\ndead ends (one application window closed with no submission\;\none 
 grant round has lapsed and is noted for next year). A\ndatabase security 
 alert for the research site was presented\nwith a prepared\, scoped fix 
 and two routing options\; nothing\nwas changed\, awaiting the user's 
 choice. A set of partner\noutreach drafts for a grant application due 
 later this month\nwas completed\; nothing was sent\, so the remaining gap 
 is a\nsending decision\, not writing.
DTSTAMP:20261108T172913Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261015T110000
DURATION:PT15M
SUMMARY:Search Console indexing run blocked on two-step verification
UID:87c39a74-b2ef-489b-8d69-1a8f199488d7@87c3.org
DESCRIPTION:The daily indexing run signed in but stopped at the phone\ntwo-
 step prompt\; the property was never reached\, no\ninspections or requests
  were made\, and quota was untouched.\nThe remaining unverified list is 
 unchanged from the prior\nday. The run resumes once the user approves the 
 prompt\, or\nretries fresh at the next daily window.
DTSTAMP:20261108T172913Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261015T134500
DURATION:PT1H
SUMMARY:Kraft Heinz application submitted
UID:e5719d6c-8675-4d49-8216-4523a6a62a28@e571.org
DESCRIPTION:At the user's direct instruction\, an application for an 
 AI\ngovernance role was submitted. The employer portal account\nproved not
  to exist (an earlier form fill had never been tied\nto an account)\; a 
 new account was created using the portal's\nemail-code sign-in only\, the 
 application was refilled from the\nrecord with the tailored resume\, and 
 submission was confirmed\non the portal dashboard the same day. A seven-
 day follow-up\nis due. The account record notes that no password exists 
 for\nthis portal.
DTSTAMP:20261108T172913Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261015T133700
DURATION:PT45M
SUMMARY:North York General Hospital application: package built\, posting 
 verified
UID:105135ca-5d66-43ad-8d32-5ae65c9a4804@1051.org
DESCRIPTION:At the user's direction\, a tailored application package 
 was\nbuilt for a hospital analytics consultant role and shown to\nhim for 
 approval. The user personally cleared the portal's\nbot checks\, and the 
 live posting was verified in full\,\nincluding its early-November closing 
 date. Submission awaits\nonly his approval tap.
DTSTAMP:20261108T172913Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261015T161900
DURATION:PT45M
SUMMARY:Special job search\, Indeed step: Toronto pass completed
UID:86a4230c-8092-4e3a-bf0a-f78f3fc50b0e@86a4.org
DESCRIPTION:The earlier parked Indeed task was found dead at 
 its\nverification check. A fresh task\, spawned so the user could\nclear 
 that check himself\, completed the whole Toronto pass\nwith the check 
 never appearing. Ten candidates were verified\non their postings\, seven 
 of them new and all in the stable\ntrack\; the remaining cities and the 
 remote pass are still\nto run.
DTSTAMP:20261108T172913Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261015T161800
DURATION:PT20M
SUMMARY:Application documents self-reviewed: all nine proofed\, one flaw 
 fixed
UID:ab0b31f7-bd71-4695-b0b8-23e4ea6abadb@ab0b.org
DESCRIPTION:At the user's request\, all nine application package 
 documents\nacross four employers received a dedicated proof 
 pass:\nspelling\, facts against the master record\, employer and 
 role\ndetails\, and layout. All were verified clean\, with honest\nskill 
 boundaries confirmed throughout. One flaw was found\nand fixed: an 
 inconsistent date in one resume\, after which\nthat package was rebuilt 
 and re-verified.
DTSTAMP:20261108T172913Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261015T164700
DURATION:PT1H
SUMMARY:Halton Region application submitted ahead of deadline
UID:8f6a2708-0e12-49dc-a21d-93c5f7a0d542@8f6a.org
DESCRIPTION:The regional quality improvement application was submitted 
 a\nday ahead of its deadline. The day's path: an initial sign-in\nwas 
 rejected\, a user-approved password reset produced no\nemail\, and the 
 account-creation verification route was\nretried\; the portal's protected 
 code entry proved unusable\,\nand verification finally succeeded under the
  user's explicit\nrepeated direction. The application was completed from 
 the\nrecord\, a parser-created duplicate education row was deleted\nrather
  than left as a false credential\, and the submission\nconfirmation was 
 received on-page. A seven-day follow-up\nis due.
DTSTAMP:20261108T172913Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261015T171300
DURATION:PT30M
SUMMARY:LHSC application launched
UID:8b41dd9e-954d-49d4-9064-e211b7b55eb7@8b41.org
DESCRIPTION:Immediately after the Halton submission\, the application 
 for\na hospital decision support consultant role closing the next\nday was
  launched\, with the tailored resume and cover letter\nand the full answer
  set pre-loaded from the record. Status at\nday's flush: registration and 
 submission in progress\, outcome\nnot yet reported.
DTSTAMP:20261108T172913Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261015T170000
DURATION:PT15M
SUMMARY:Icarus appraisal replies watch: no new replies
UID:0839d9e9-801a-4a44-9adb-c4bda95e3ddc@0839.org
DESCRIPTION:The replies watch checked the mailbox live for responses 
 from\nthe auction houses and appraiser contacted about the bronze.\nNo new
  replies: one house has declined\, one is still\nreviewing\, and the 
 remaining parties are still silent. No\nestimate has been received yet and
  the watch continues.
DTSTAMP:20261108T172913Z
END:VEVENT
