 desk\; the brand campaigns belong to a colleague) and\nruled that 
 superseded rotation groups are paused\, never\ndeleted\, so their keywords
  and history survive. A\nsearch-terms audit of nearly a thousand terms 
 found the\njunk traffic arrives mainly through AI expansion beyond\nthe 
 keyword lists. Execution\, all verified live: the\nbroad-match auto-apply 
 was turned off\; the nine legacy\ngroups were paused\; negatives were 
 added for a symptom\ncluster\, an election-poll cluster\, a piracy-list 
 phrase\nand one exact term\; AI Max was turned off for the 
 Target\ncampaign only. The platform refused two negatives because\nthose 
 terms are targeted keywords inside their own group\;\nremoving them is the
  owner's pending decision. Keyword\nlists for the seven Paper groups found
  holding zero\nkeywords were presented for approval\; nothing loaded yet.
